node_modules
.svelte-kit
build
.netlify
.vercel
.output
.vite

# Environment. Everything except the committed example, which holds names only
# and never a value.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Installed agent skills. Reinstalled per machine, not project history.
# Note the trailing `/*` rather than `/`: git will not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a `!` re-include beneath `.claude/` can never match. Excluding
# the contents instead is what makes the agents exception below work.
.claude/*

# ...except the model-pinned subagent definitions. These are not a per-machine
# install: they are the project's cost architecture, and every one of them
# carries the reasoning for its tier. Untracked, a clone or a wiped .claude/
# silently reverts every subagent to the session model, and the only symptom is
# the bill. Companion to _bmad/custom/bmad-*.toml.
!.claude/agents/
.claude/agents/*
!.claude/agents/*.md

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.local
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Real Fantrax exports. Kept out of git deliberately: they are league data, not
# source — thirty-one files of real Managers' rosters, salaries and contract
# lengths. The repository needs the ADAPTER to be correct (see
# src/lib/adapters/fantrax/ and tests/adapters/), never the data itself, and a
# committed export would go stale the moment the league transacts.
team_rosters/
